 .B \-1
 Limit the search to a single result and quit immediately. This is an alias for '--max-results=1'.
 .TP
+.B \-\-count
+Print the number of search results instead of the results themselves, followed by a newline. All other search options still apply,
+and '--max-results' or '-1' cap the count. Cannot be combined with -x/--exec, -X/--exec-batch, -l/--list-details, --format,
+-0/--print0 or -q/--quiet.
+.TP
 .B \-q, \-\-quiet
 When the flag is present, the program does not print anything and will instead exit with a code of 0 if there is at least one search result.
 Otherwise, the exit code will be 1.
